ua_hiding.css holds excerpts of the user-agent rules of three specifications, selected and
arranged by scripts/vendor_ua_hiding.py. The rest of evidence-judge is under the MIT License
(LICENSE); these excerpts remain under their own licences.

HTML Standard, section "Rendering" (user-agent stylesheet rules that hide elements)
  https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/rendering.html
  Copyright © WHATWG (Apple, Google, Mozilla, Microsoft).
  Licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License:
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
  Changes: only the rules that hide an element are kept, each on one line; the judge's own
  adjustments follow them, marked "evidence-judge".

MathML Core, section "User Agent Stylesheet" (rules that hide elements)
  https://w3c.github.io/mathml-core/
  Copyright © World Wide Web Consortium. W3C® liability, trademark and document use rules
  apply. Used under the W3C Software and Document License:
  https://www.w3.org/copyright/software-license/

SVG 2, definition of "never-rendered element" (the element list, written as a CSS rule)
  https://svgwg.org/svg2-draft/render.html
  Copyright © World Wide Web Consortium. Used under the W3C Software and Document License:
  https://www.w3.org/copyright/software-license/
